      "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing cynical self-deprecation",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the second part of the text ('the kind of patience it takes to deal with your shit'), which uses 'your' to directly address the viewer, implying the user is the one who needs to deal with their own shortcomings. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user identifies with the self-deprecating, cynical perspective.",
