    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b2babb43",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Cynical self-deprecation with misogynistic undertones",
      "description": "The meme uses ironic self-deprecation to undercut the initial romantic ideal of patience associated with beard growth, but the second part ('deal with your shit') implies that the man's patience is only valuable if he can handle his own flaws — which can be interpreted as a subtle, indirect dismissal of the man's character or a mocking of the romantic ideal itself. While not overtly misogynistic, the framing of 'patience' as a trait that must be earned through enduring personal flaws can be seen as undermining the value of patience as a positive trait, potentially reinforcing negative stereotypes about men's emotional maturity or self-control. The humor relies on a cynical, self-deprecating tone that may be perceived as dismissive or condescending toward the man's character or the romantic ideal.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_1961e99b"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_443d512e",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals familiar with internet humor, particularly those who appreciate ironic, self-deprecating, and satirical commentary on dating norms and romantic stereotypes. The meme appeals to a demographic that understands and engages with the cultural trope of 'beard as patience' and can relate to the cynical twist of 'deal with your shit.' This audience likely includes young adults and millennials who are active on social media, where selfie culture and dating advice memes are prevalent. The humor relies on recognizing the absurdity of romanticizing patience as a trait tied to beard growth, and the audience is expected to find the irony amusing, even if they recognize the underlying critique of societal expectations in relationships. The meme’s tone suggests it is aimed at those who are either cynical about dating or enjoy humor that subverts traditional romantic ideals.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_1961e99b"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
